          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582783,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Early Life of Bertrand Russell</strong><br>\nBertrand Russell was born into a prominent aristocratic family in Wales, United Kingdom. He was raised by his grandparents after his parents' death. Russell showed early signs of intelligence and went on to study at Cambridge University. His early life was marked by loneliness and study, which shaped his views on philosophy and logic.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Academic Achievements</strong><br>\nRussell excelled at Cambridge, focusing on mathematical logic and philosophy. He published his first book, \"An Essay on the Foundations of Geometry,\" in 1897. His academic work eventually laid the groundwork for his most famous work, \"Principia Mathematica,\" which he co-authored with Alfred North Whitehead.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Work on \"Principia Mathematica\"</strong><br>\nPrincipia Mathematica, written with Whitehead, was a monumental work in the field of logic and mathematics. Published from 1910 to 1913, it aimed to derive mathematical truths from logical axioms and principles. This work established Russell as one of the foremost logicians of his time.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "53bc5361-5ce5-43a9-a00f-57bbceee9cd0"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
